# Example 09 — NOISE.AUTO: auto-derived fd_step for noisy BFGS.
#
# LAMMPS-driven evaluations are noisy: tiny parameter changes can
# produce step-shaped jumps in the reported loss. With the default
# fd_step = 1e-6, BFGS finite differences return garbage gradients.
#
# NOISE.AUTO derives fd_step from the search-space geometry:
#   fd_step = max(1e-3 * box_diagonal / sqrt(dim), 1e-6)
# where box_diagonal is the L2 norm of (high - low) in the
# post-transform space. Hand-set `PARAM fd_step` always wins.

OPTIMIZER
  NOISE
    AUTO
  ENDNOISE
  STRATEGY
    TYPE PLAIN
    LIB DLIB
    ALGO BFGS
    MAXEVAL 6
  ENDSTRATEGY
ENDOPTIMIZER

LOSS L2
FAILSCORE 1e16
PC_ERMSE 0 0.0001
PC_LAMMPS --script ../common/lammps/Ecoh.in --varloss Ecoh 8.10 800

OPTIM RCUT2B (1) 4.0 6.0
OPTIM SGRIDMB (1) 0.1 0.4

OUTPUT 1
BOUTPUT 1
